    "body": "## What does this implement/fix?\n\n| Property | Value |\n|---|---|\n| Method | `createLanHttpClient` |\n| Class | `io.github.stardomains3.oxproxion.ChatViewModel` |\n| File | `app/src/main/java/io/github/stardomains3/oxproxion/ChatViewModel.kt` |\n| Specification | `TLSCertificateValidationSpec` |\n| Analysis tool | `static:manual` |\n\n## Summary\n\n### Observed dynamic-analysis failure\n\nThe dynamic-analysis run by `static:manual` reported (`TLSCertificateValidationSpec`) while exercising `io.github.stardomains3.oxproxion.ChatViewModel.createLanHttpClient`:\n\n> Static candidate (not executed): the client used for the user-configured LAN endpoint installs an X509TrustManager with an empty checkServerTrusted and hostnameVerifier { _, _ -> true }, and requests on it send 'Authorization: Bearer <LAN API key>' (CWE-295).\n\n### Root cause\n\ncreateLanHttpClient installs a no-op X509TrustManager into an SSLContext, passes that trust manager and derived socket factory to the OkHttp configuration, and supplies a hostname verifier that always returns true. These source-level configuration choices defeat the certificate-chain and hostname-validation predicates reported as TrustAllCertificates.\n\n### Correction strategy\n\nRemove the permissive custom TLS configuration and rely on the platform/OkHttp default certificate-chain and hostname validation. Do not retain a broad trust-all exception. If supported LAN deployments require non-public certificates, select a narrowly scoped, review-approved trust model rather than disabling validation globally.\n\n### Coordinated changes\n\n- `app/src/main/java/io/github/stardomains3/oxproxion/ChatViewModel.kt`: Eliminates the no-op X509TrustManager, custom SSLContext, custom socket factory, and unconditional hostname verifier so LAN HTTPS requests use OkHttp/platform certificate-chain and hostname validation defaults. Retains the existing factory name and all non-TLS configuration.\n- `app/src/test/java/io/github/stardomains3/oxproxion/ChatViewModelTlsConfigurationTest.kt`: Adds the planned deterministic JVM source-level regression test without requiring a ChatViewModel instance, network access, or dependencies beyond declared JUnit and Java/Kotlin APIs. It validates the coordinated production contract specifically within createLanHttpClient.\n\n### Verification included\n\n- Run the patched module Gradle build and JVM unit-test task, including ChatViewModelTlsConfigurationTest.\n- Compile the patched module's androidTest sources.\n- Run ChatViewModelTlsConfigurationTest as the deterministic source-level recheck that createLanHttpClient has no no-op trust manager, permissive socket-factory configuration, or always-true hostname verifier.\n- Run the patched module Gradle JVM unit-test task, including ChatViewModelTlsConfigurationTest.\n\n## How was this tested?\n\n- [x] Automated test coverage added in 1 test file(s)\n- [x] Project compiles successfully (`:app:testDebugUnitTest`)\n- [ ] Confirmed by a project maintainer\n\n## Additional context\n\nI’m an undergraduate Computer Engineering student at the University of Brasília (UnB), and this contribution is part of a research project involving static analysis of Android apps.\n\nI’m happy to adjust the implementation to better match the project’s architecture, coding conventions, or maintainers’ recommendations.",
